1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,571
The first thing Umbrella ever lost, it lost on a wet
motorway in England at two o'clock

2
00:00:13,591 --> 00:00:14,570
in the morning.

3
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:20,956
A refrigerated lorry carrying four hundred litres of
Aeterna intermediate from a contract

4
00:00:20,976 --> 00:00:26,895
plant near Cambridge to the port at Felixstowe was
stopped by a broken-down van, boarded

5
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:33,036
by six men in under ninety seconds, driven eleven
miles, and emptied into a second vehicle.

6
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:39,042
The driver was not hurt. The cargo was worth, at the
black-market price a European clinic

7
00:00:39,062 --> 00:00:42,551
was quietly paying, about forty-one
million dollars.

8
00:00:42,951 --> 00:00:48,915
The Essex police were competent and quick and found the
second vehicle burned out by Thursday.

9
00:00:48,935 --> 00:00:50,761
They never found the product.

10
00:00:51,161 --> 00:00:57,478
Wesker read the incident report at six in the
morning and did not react to any of the

11
00:00:57,498 --> 00:01:00,311
parts of it that upset his executives.

12
00:01:00,832 --> 00:01:05,121
(flat) The loss is insured. The insurer
will pay within ninety days.

13
00:01:05,522 --> 00:01:10,192
The loss is not the problem. The problem is that we
are in forty-one countries with seven

14
00:01:10,212 --> 00:01:15,040
hundred cold-chain movements a month and we are
protected by whatever local firm the freight

15
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:19,625
forwarder happened to hire. Umbrella has no security
function. It has a man called Hale

16
00:01:19,645 --> 00:01:22,735
and twenty-two people who guard four
buildings in Delaware.

17
00:01:23,135 --> 00:01:25,965
You are both discussing the
wrong incident.

18
00:01:26,364 --> 00:01:27,984
He put the tablet down.

19
00:01:28,504 --> 00:01:33,147
They knew the route, the schedule and the temperature
spec. They knew which of two lorries

20
00:01:33,167 --> 00:01:38,120
was worth taking. That is not opportunism; that is
procurement. Somebody bought that information

21
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:42,627
from inside this company, and everything we have
said since page one of that report has

22
00:01:42,647 --> 00:01:43,715
been about the lorry.

23
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:46,759
You want an internal investigation.

24
00:01:47,159 --> 00:01:52,061
I want an *instrument*. I have been running a global
pharmaceutical concern with a night

25
00:01:52,081 --> 00:01:54,689
watchman and a locksmith. That
ends this month.

26
00:01:55,090 --> 00:02:00,902
He put eighty thousand Points into the Company
banner and pulled forty times, and the

27
00:02:00,922 --> 00:02:07,145
first thirty-nine produced exactly what the odds said
they would: commons, a vehicle fleet,

28
00:02:07,165 --> 00:02:13,183
two cohorts of security officers, an Uncommon that
turned out to be a logistics planning

29
00:02:13,203 --> 00:02:19,427
suite, and a Rare that was a third Tyrant, which he
sent to Arklay's cryogenic hall without

30
00:02:19,447 --> 00:02:20,799
particular interest.

31
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:23,249
The fortieth pull came up violet.

32
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:32,006
Epic. Operator and doctrine. Designation: Hunk.
Grade: sole survivor, special operations

33
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:39,805
command. The package includes a training pipeline, a
selection standard, a tactics library

34
00:02:39,825 --> 00:02:47,777
and an equipment specification. Any security cohort you
own may be brought to this standard.

35
00:02:48,367 --> 00:02:54,292
He arrived at Arklay the following morning in a
black transport with no markings, and

36
00:02:54,312 --> 00:02:58,697
he came up the steps in a gas mask, and
he did not take it off.

37
00:02:59,217 --> 00:03:00,907
(radio) Director.

38
00:03:01,307 --> 00:03:03,113
Is there a face under that?

39
00:03:03,513 --> 00:03:05,203
(radio) Yes, sir.

40
00:03:05,603 --> 00:03:08,120
Do you intend to show it to anyone?

41
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,170
(radio) No, sir.

42
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:12,737
Excellent. Neither do I.

43
00:03:13,138 --> 00:03:19,324
The narrator will note that in nineteen years of
service, in four continents and one ocean

44
00:03:19,344 --> 00:03:25,394
and eventually in vacuum, no photograph of HUNK's
face was ever taken, and that this was

45
00:03:25,414 --> 00:03:31,601
not a System effect. It was a preference, and Wesker
respected it the way one professional

46
00:03:31,621 --> 00:03:33,807
respects another's superstition.

47
00:03:34,207 --> 00:03:40,367
The Umbrella Security Service was founded on the
eleventh of November 2028 with two hundred

48
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:46,207
and eighty personnel, of whom two hundred and
forty-one were Absolute, and its command

49
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:49,805
structure was drawn on a whiteboard
in forty minutes.

50
00:03:50,205 --> 00:03:57,166
Hale commanded it. Hale was Absolute, incapable of
doubt, incapable of ambition, and therefore

51
00:03:57,186 --> 00:04:03,553
the only man alive whom Wesker was willing to give
two hundred and eighty armed people

52
00:04:03,573 --> 00:04:03,775
to.

53
00:04:04,175 --> 00:04:10,321
HUNK ran operations, which is a different job, and
the difference is the entire reason

54
00:04:10,341 --> 00:04:12,185
Umbrella never had a coup.

55
00:04:12,705 --> 00:04:14,904
Mr. Hale. Your doctrine.

56
00:04:15,305 --> 00:04:20,917
(flat) Deterrence by presence. Visible protection at
every site. Response within eleven

57
00:04:20,937 --> 00:04:21,435
minutes.

58
00:04:21,834 --> 00:04:24,745
Wrong. Try again, using Mr.
HUNK's material.

59
00:04:25,144 --> 00:04:30,394
(radio) No presence. No response. Interdiction
before the event, by knowing the event

60
00:04:30,414 --> 00:04:31,014
is coming.

61
00:04:31,415 --> 00:04:36,125
Yes. I do not want guards, Mr. Hale. Guards are a
tax I pay for ever, and a guard tells

62
00:04:36,145 --> 00:04:40,911
the world where the valuable thing is. I want a
company that appears to have no security

63
00:04:40,931 --> 00:04:45,805
at all, and a very small number of people who arrive
fifteen hours before a thing happens.

64
00:04:46,204 --> 00:04:52,021
That was the doctrine. It never changed. Thirty
years later, when the Umbrella Security

65
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:58,058
Service was a hundred and ninety thousand strong and
had regiments in orbit, that sentence

66
00:04:58,078 --> 00:05:00,675
was still the first line of the manual.

67
00:05:01,074 --> 00:05:06,615
The narrator would like one scene with Hale, who has
been in this story since the lobby

68
00:05:06,635 --> 00:05:09,748
in Chapter One and has said
perhaps twenty words.

69
00:05:10,148 --> 00:05:16,267
Wesker found him at two in the morning standing in a
corridor outside the armoury, doing

70
00:05:16,287 --> 00:05:22,338
nothing, which is what the Absolute did when they
had no instruction and nowhere to be.

71
00:05:22,858 --> 00:05:25,535
How long have you been standing
here, Mr. Hale?

72
00:05:25,935 --> 00:05:28,085
(flat) Four hours, Director.

73
00:05:28,485 --> 00:05:29,515
Doing what?

74
00:05:29,915 --> 00:05:31,625
(flat) Waiting, sir.

75
00:05:32,024 --> 00:05:33,980
(very cold) For what?

76
00:05:34,821 --> 00:05:37,151
(flat) I hadn't got that far, sir.

77
00:05:37,550 --> 00:05:43,150
The narrator asks you to sit with that, because it
is the clearest description anybody

78
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:48,770
ever gives of what the Absolute were, and it is
given by one of them, cheerfully, in a

79
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:50,860
corridor, at two in the morning.

80
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:55,958
Mr. Hale, I am going to give you a standing
instruction and it will be the only one of

81
00:05:55,978 --> 00:06:00,503
its kind in this organisation. When you have
nothing to do, you will do something you

82
00:06:00,523 --> 00:06:05,047
have chosen. Anything at all. Read, walk, sleep,
take the car out. I do not care what

83
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:06,490
it is and I will never ask.

84
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,990
(flat) Yes, sir.

85
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:12,610
(flat) Director — may I ask what
I should choose?

86
00:06:13,011 --> 00:06:18,006
(very cold) No. That is the entire point of the
instruction and it is why it will not

87
00:06:18,026 --> 00:06:18,301
work.

88
00:06:18,701 --> 00:06:24,428
It did not work. Hale complied, as he complied with
everything: for nineteen years he

89
00:06:24,448 --> 00:06:30,582
went for a walk at the same time every night, four
kilometres, the same route, and reported

90
00:06:30,602 --> 00:06:36,465
nothing, and enjoyed nothing, and when he was
released in the seventh cohort in 2085 at

91
00:06:36,485 --> 00:06:41,131
the age of eighty-one the first thing he
did was walk the same route.

92
00:06:41,531 --> 00:06:47,108
He walked it for another nine years. Then, in 2094,
at eighty-nine, he stopped, and went

93
00:06:47,128 --> 00:06:53,214
a different way, and got lost, and the Directorate's duty
officer received a call at twenty-nine

94
00:06:53,234 --> 00:06:59,001
at night from a man who had been the head of its
security service for forty years, standing

95
00:06:59,021 --> 00:07:04,408
at a road junction four kilometres from his house,
saying — and it is in the log, and

96
00:07:04,428 --> 00:07:08,605
Wesker read it, and the log records that
he read it eleven times —

97
00:07:09,125 --> 00:07:14,713
I don't know where I am. It's all right. I did it
on purpose. Could somebody come and

98
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:15,175
get me?

99
00:07:15,574 --> 00:07:21,264
The internal leak took Pell nine days and an audit of
who had opened which routing file.

100
00:07:21,665 --> 00:07:27,691
It was not a traitor. That is worth saying, because
Wesker had expected one and had already

101
00:07:27,711 --> 00:07:33,804
decided what to do about it. It was a
twenty-six-year-old logistics coordinator in Rotterdam

102
00:07:33,824 --> 00:07:39,452
named Bram de Vos who had been socially engineered
over four months by a very patient

103
00:07:39,472 --> 00:07:45,100
woman at a conference, and who was, when Hale's
people finally sat down opposite him,

104
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,626
so relieved to be caught that he wept.

105
00:07:48,026 --> 00:07:53,768
The woman worked for a private laboratory near Leuven
that had been buying stolen biologics

106
00:07:53,788 --> 00:07:58,074
for nineteen years and reselling them to
clinics in three countries.

107
00:07:58,473 --> 00:08:03,524
The Belgian authorities would have taken nineteen
months and would probably have won.

108
00:08:04,043 --> 00:08:06,560
Mr. HUNK. How long would you need?

109
00:08:06,961 --> 00:08:10,911
(radio) Twenty-two minutes on the ground.
Four days of preparation.

110
00:08:11,310 --> 00:08:12,940
Nobody is harmed.

111
00:08:13,341 --> 00:08:14,991
(radio) Understood.

112
00:08:15,391 --> 00:08:20,582
I mean it precisely, Mr. HUNK. Not one person. Not a
broken wrist, not a frightened night

113
00:08:20,602 --> 00:08:26,086
porter with a story. If a single human being in that
building requires a doctor, the operation

114
00:08:26,106 --> 00:08:28,721
has failed regardless of what
you bring back.

115
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,011
(radio) Understood, sir.

116
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:36,932
The narrator will tell you how it went, beat by
beat, because it is the first time in

117
00:08:36,952 --> 00:08:42,931
this story that Umbrella's hand touches the world
directly and because everything it becomes

118
00:08:42,951 --> 00:08:44,561
is already visible in it.

119
00:08:44,961 --> 00:08:50,835
At one thirty-eight the site's alarm contract
lapsed. Not was disabled — *lapsed*, in

120
00:08:50,855 --> 00:08:56,730
the monitoring company's records, due to an unpaid
invoice, four days earlier, with a

121
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:57,771
letter on file.

122
00:08:58,171 --> 00:09:03,949
At one forty the night porter, a sixty-year-old man
named Luc, received a call from his

123
00:09:03,969 --> 00:09:09,947
supervisor telling him a gas leak had been reported on
the estate and that he should stand

124
00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:15,745
at the main gate until the utility arrived. He stood
at the main gate. He was there for

125
00:09:15,765 --> 00:09:18,211
the entire operation and saw nothing.

126
00:09:18,610 --> 00:09:24,534
At one forty-one, six people in black entered through
a service door that had been fitted

127
00:09:24,554 --> 00:09:30,210
with a new lock in October by a contractor nobody
at the laboratory could later name.

128
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:37,312
At one fifty-two they were in the cold store. At two
hundred and one, four hundred litres

129
00:09:37,332 --> 00:09:43,730
of Aeterna intermediate, still in Umbrella's own
drums, went into a refrigerated van.

130
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:49,719
At two hundred and four, HUNK stopped in the
laboratory's server room for ninety seconds

131
00:09:49,739 --> 00:09:52,650
and copied nineteen years of
purchase records.

132
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:59,182
At two hundred and six they were gone. Total time
on the ground: twenty-five minutes.

133
00:09:59,202 --> 00:10:03,091
Injuries: none. Shots fired: none.
Doors broken: none.

134
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:09,955
At nine o'clock that morning the laboratory's director
arrived to find an empty cold store,

135
00:10:09,975 --> 00:10:16,511
a functioning alarm system that had been off for four
days, and no sign of entry whatsoever.

136
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:22,327
He did not call the police. He could not call the
police, because the nineteen years of

137
00:10:22,347 --> 00:10:27,701
purchase records in his server room explained
exactly where the product had come from.

138
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:34,246
Two months later, an anonymous package of those records
reached the Belgian federal prosecutor,

139
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:40,152
and the laboratory's directors were arrested in April,
and Umbrella's name appeared nowhere

140
00:10:40,172 --> 00:10:40,931
in the file.

141
00:10:42,081 --> 00:10:50,343
Acting with intelligence. Forty-one million dollars
recovered. Adversary removed by lawful

142
00:10:50,363 --> 00:10:58,350
process, unattributed. No injuries. No records. One
hundred and eighty thousand Points.

143
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:05,155
Wesker had watched the whole thing from Wilmington on
the Surveillance Suite he had pulled

144
00:11:05,175 --> 00:11:11,529
out of a lottery eighteen months earlier, and he had
said four words in twenty-five minutes.

145
00:11:11,928 --> 00:11:14,558
The four words were: *"Not the
second door."*

146
00:11:14,958 --> 00:11:16,688
In the silence, the passenger.

147
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:18,438
You enjoyed that.

148
00:11:18,839 --> 00:11:19,689
I did.

149
00:11:20,089 --> 00:11:21,577
It was a burglary.

150
00:11:21,976 --> 00:11:26,673
It was a *demonstration*. Twenty-five minutes, no blood,
no record, and a competitor destroyed

151
00:11:26,693 --> 00:11:30,988
by his own paperwork four months later in a court he
chose to be in. Do you understand

152
00:11:31,008 --> 00:11:35,705
what that is worth? Every intelligence service in Europe
will read the Belgian file eventually

153
00:11:35,725 --> 00:11:40,071
and find nothing in it. Nothing at all. And the
nothing will be so clean that a certain

154
00:11:40,091 --> 00:11:41,726
kind of professional will sit up.

155
00:11:42,126 --> 00:11:43,827
You want them to sit up.

156
00:11:44,229 --> 00:11:48,919
I want exactly nine people in the world to sit up,
and I want all nine of them to work

157
00:11:48,939 --> 00:11:53,739
for governments, and I want every one of them to
conclude, privately, that whatever this

158
00:11:53,759 --> 00:11:57,519
is, it is not worth the career of the man
who says it out loud first.

159
00:11:57,918 --> 00:12:01,328
The narrator notes that seven of the
nine did exactly that.

160
00:12:01,729 --> 00:12:07,310
The eighth was a woman in Beijing, and she waited
three years and then asked him to lunch.

161
00:12:07,708 --> 00:12:13,369
The ninth was an FBI supervisory special agent in
Philadelphia named Owen Carrick, who

162
00:12:13,389 --> 00:12:18,984
at that moment was in the fourth month of a case
about a company with no construction

163
00:12:19,004 --> 00:12:24,664
records, and who did not know yet that he had
already made the decision that would end

164
00:12:24,684 --> 00:12:27,439
his career and begin the rest of his life.

165
00:12:27,839 --> 00:12:33,642
By Christmas the Umbrella Security Service was four
hundred strong and had begun to look

166
00:12:33,662 --> 00:12:35,429
like the thing it would be.

167
00:12:35,828 --> 00:12:41,740
They trained at Arklay, in the forest, in weather.
They wore black without insignia. The

168
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:47,671
Absolute among them — and by December that was nine
in ten — did not speak in formation,

169
00:12:47,691 --> 00:12:53,198
did not shift their weight, and did not blink at
the rate that human beings blink.

170
00:12:53,599 --> 00:12:59,654
And on the twentieth of December a Tyrant walked
through the hangar on its way from the

171
00:12:59,674 --> 00:13:06,009
transport to the cryogenic lift: two point nine
metres, grey, silent, entirely indifferent.

172
00:13:06,408 --> 00:13:11,239
Four hundred trained soldiers watched it go
past. Not one of them moved.

173
00:13:11,639 --> 00:13:17,599
HUNK — who had, according to a System panel nobody
but Wesker could read, been through

174
00:13:17,619 --> 00:13:23,579
twenty-seven things that would break a man, and who
feared nothing in any useful sense

175
00:13:23,599 --> 00:13:27,473
of the word — stepped one pace to his
left as it passed.

176
00:13:27,874 --> 00:13:33,735
Wesker saw it from the gallery. He did not mention
it for nineteen years, and then he

177
00:13:33,755 --> 00:13:39,894
mentioned it once, in a conversation in orbit with a
woman who had been afraid of nothing

178
00:13:39,914 --> 00:13:42,524
for even longer, and what he said was:

179
00:13:43,043 --> 00:13:48,047
Everything alive gets out of its way. That is not
obedience and it is not fear. It is

180
00:13:48,067 --> 00:13:53,071
arithmetic. And the day I stop being the thing that
decides where it walks, I will be

181
00:13:53,091 --> 00:13:54,193
the arithmetic too.
